# Update Plugin Version Workflow

When the user says **update plugin version** (or equivalent: bump version, cut a release version), perform **all three** operations in order. Do not stop after only bumping the version number.

## 1. Update plugin version

Bump the patch (or as directed) in every version source of truth:

- [`gradle.properties`](gradle.properties) — `pluginVersion`
- [`zide-plugin.xml`](zide-plugin.xml) — `version` attribute and download URL (`V{version}` / zip name)
- [`.cursor/rules/project-knowledge.mdc`](.cursor/rules/project-knowledge.mdc) — Current Version line if present

Default bump: patch (`0.0.N` → `0.0.N+1`) unless the user specifies minor/major.

## 2. Add the changelog on the plugin

Document notable changes since the previous version in **both**:

- [`CHANGELOG.md`](CHANGELOG.md) — new `## [X.Y.Z] — YYYY-MM-DD` section (Added / Fixed / Changed as appropriate)
- [`src/main/resources/META-INF/plugin.xml`](src/main/resources/META-INF/plugin.xml) — prepend a `<b>X.Y.Z</b>` + `<ul>` block inside `<change-notes>`

Derive bullets from `git log` / diffs since the last version tag or previous changelog section. Keep entries user-facing and concise.

## 3. Draft a git release note

In the reply to the user, draft a GitHub release body matching the **V0.0.8** style (tag/title `V{version}`). Use this structure:

```markdown
## ZIDE IntelliJ Plugin v{version}

IntelliJ IDEA plugin for Zoho ZIDE workflows — project create, Tomcat lifecycle, deploy sync, and debug.

**Requires:** IntelliJ IDEA 2024.3+ (Community or Ultimate)

### Highlights

- **Short headline** — one-line benefit (3 bullets typical)

### What's new

#### Debug
- bullet…

#### Compiler / deploy sync
- bullet…

#### New project / create
- bullet… (omit empty sections)

### Install

1. Download `zide-intelliJ-plugin-{version}.zip` from this release
2. IntelliJ → **Settings → Plugins → ⚙️ → Install Plugin from Disk…**
3. Select the zip → restart the IDE

### Notes

- recovery / environment caveats if relevant
```

Do **not** use a bare Summary + Test plan checklist unless the user asks. Do **not** create a git tag, GitHub release, or commit unless the user explicitly asks.

## After the three steps

Run `./gradlew clean buildPlugin` so the distributable matches the new version. Report the zip path when done.
